{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "2CO",
  "chapter": 11,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I earnestly wish ye could bear with me a little in ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " folly: and indeed bear with me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I am jealous over you with godly jealousy: for I have espoused you to one husband, that I may present ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "you as",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a chaste virgin to Christ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But I fear, lest by any means, as the serpent beguiled Eve through his subtilty, so your minds should be corrupted from the simplicity that is in Christ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For if he that cometh preacheth another Jesus, whom we have not preached, or ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "if",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ye receive another spirit, which ye have not received, or another gospel, which ye have not accepted, ye might well bear with ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I suppose I was not a whit behind the very greatest apostles.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But though ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "I am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " rude in speech, yet not in knowledge; but we have been thoroughly made manifest among you in all things.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Have I committed an offense in abasing myself that ye might be exalted, because I have preached to you the gospel of God without reward?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I robbed other churches, taking wages ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", to do you service.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And when I was present with you, and wanted, I was chargeable to no man: for that which was lacking to me the brethren who came from Macedonia supplied: and in all ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "things",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I have kept myself from being burdensome to you, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "so",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " will I keep ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "myself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As the truth of Christ is in me, no man shall stop me of this boasting in the regions of Achaia.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why? because I love you not? God knoweth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But what I do, that I will do, that I may cut off occasion from them who desire occasion; that in what they glory, they may be found even as we.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For such ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " false apostles, deceitful workers, transforming themselves into the apostles of Christ.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And no wonder; for Satan himself is transformed into an angel of light.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no great thing if his ministers also are transformed as the ministers of righteousness; whose end shall be according to their works.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I say again, Let no man think me a fool; if otherwise, yet as a fool receive me, that I may boast myself a little.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "That which I speak, I speak ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not according to the Lord, but as it were foolishly, in this confidence of boasting.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Seeing that many glory after the flesh, I will glory also.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For ye suffer fools gladly, seeing ye ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "yourselves",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " are wise.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For ye suffer, if a man bringeth you into bondage, if a man devoureth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "you",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", if a man taketh ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "from you",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", if a man exalteth himself, if a man smiteth you on the face.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I speak as concerning reproach, as though we had been weak. But in whatever respect any is bold, (I speak foolishly) I am bold also.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Are they Hebrews? so ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I. Are they Israelites? so ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I. Are they the offspring of Abraham? so ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Are they ministers of Christ? (I speak as a fool) I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " more; in labors more abundant, in stripes above measure, in prisons more frequent, in deaths often.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "From the Jews five times I received forty ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "stripes",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " save one.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thrice was I beaten with rods, once I was stoned, thrice I suffered shipwreck, a night and a day I have been in the deep;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " journeyings often, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " perils of waters, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " perils of robbers, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " perils by ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my own",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " countrymen, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " perils by the heathen, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " perils in the city, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " perils in the wilderness, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " perils in the sea, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " perils among false brethren;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In weariness and painfulness, in watchings often, in hunger and thirst, in fastings often, in cold and nakedness.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Besides those things that are without, that which cometh upon me daily, the care of all the churches.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who is weak, and I am not weak? who is made to fall into sin, and I burn not?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If I must needs glory, I will glory of the things which concern my infirmities.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The God and Father of our Lord Jesus Christ, who is blessed for evermore, knoweth that I lie not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In Damascus the governor under Aretas the king kept the city of the Damascenes with a garrison, desirous to apprehend me:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "2CO.11.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:2CO.11.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And through a window in a basket I was let down by the wall, and escaped his hands.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
